  "answers": {
    "Qwen2.5-VL-7B": {
      "What is the recommended maximum spacing for channelizing devices in intermediate-term situations (Note 4)?": "10 feet [3 m]",
      "Does the 'STAKE SPACING TABLE' provide spacing requirements for slopes steeper than 1V:2H (e.g., 1V:1H)?": "No, the 'STAKE SPACING TABLE' does not provide spacing requirements for slopes steeper than 1V:2H (e.g., 1V:1H). The table only lists spacings for slopes up to 1V:6H.",
      "According to General Note 3 for underdrains and edge drains, what is the minimum width requirement for the trench relative to the outlet pipe?": "The minimum width requirement for the trench relative to the outlet pipe is 2 inches (50 mm) wider than the outlet pipe.",
      "In the 'HALF ROAD CLOSURE ON MULTI-LANE HIGHWAYS' diagram, how is the 'WORK ZONE' area visually distinguished?": "The 'WORK ZONE' area in the 'HALF ROAD CLOSURE ON MULTI-LANE HIGHWAYS' diagram is visually distinguished by a shaded or hatched pattern within the work zone limits.",
      "What is the specified height for the 'V-MESH END STRIPS' shown in the 'EXPANDED VIEW'?": "The specified height for the 'V-MESH END STRIPS' shown in the 'EXPANDED VIEW' is 4'-10\" [1.5 m].",
      "According to the 'STAKE LENGTH' table, what is the required stake length for sandy soil?": "6 ft [1.8 m]",
      "According to the 'STANDARD GABION SIZES' table, what is the Unit Capacity (CY) for a 12 ft x 3 ft x 3 ft gabion?": "4.0 CY",
      "What internal component is shown dividing the 'GABION' and 'REVET MATTRESS' units into smaller cells?": "DIAPHRAGMS",
      "In the 'LACING DETAIL FOR WIRE ENCLOSED RIPRAP', what is the specific gage of the smooth steel wire used for edge ties?": "12 1/2 GAGE [2.5 THICK]",
      "What reinforcement is shown surrounding the valve box in the 'VALVE BOX COLLAR' plan view?": "The reinforcement shown surrounding the valve box in the 'VALVE BOX COLLAR' plan view is #4 [#13] COATED REBAR.",
      "What is the specified spacing for the 'Sequential Chevron' devices in the tapering section?": "The specified spacing for the 'Sequential Chevron' devices in the tapering section is 24 inches (60 cm).",
      "According to the 'RODENT SCREEN DETAIL', what is the specific wire diameter required for the hardware cloth?": "The specific wire diameter required for the hardware cloth in the 'RODENT SCREEN DETAIL' is 0.025 inches (0.635 mm).",
      "In the 'LACING DETAIL', what is the maximum spacing for the hog rings used as an alternative to lacing?": "4 inches (100 mm)",
      "According to the diagrams and Note 3, how many outlets are required if a sag (low) point exists along a run of edge drain?": "2",
      "According to the 'ALTERNATE PRECAST STILLING BASIN' Top View, what is the width of the basin at the pipe opening end?": "The width of the basin at the pipe opening end is 4 inches (100 mm).",
      "Based on General Note 2 for underdrains and edge drains, how is payment handled for underdrain and edge drain outlet appurtenances?": "Payment for underdrain and edge drain outlet appurtenances is not paid for separately; they are considered incidental to the underdrain or edge drain.",
      "According to the 'GUIDELINES FOR TAPER LENGTHS' table on Sheet 2, what is the required 'Buffer Length' for a speed limit of 50 MPH?": "425[130m]",
      "Does the 'GUIDELINES FOR TAPER LENGTHS' table provide data for speed limits of 75 MPH?": "No, the 'GUIDELINES FOR TAPER LENGTHS' table does not provide data for speed limits of 75 MPH. The highest speed limit listed in the table is 70 MPH.",
      "What is the specified slope percentage for the 'Underdrain Pipe (Non-Perforated)' leading to the outlet?": "The specified slope percentage for the 'Underdrain Pipe (Non-Perforated)' leading to the outlet is 1V:10H.",
      "What is the specific tensile strength required for the 12 1/2 gage smooth steel wire used for lacing?": "The specific tensile strength required for the 12 1/2 gage smooth steel wire used for lacing is not explicitly stated in the provided images. The images only mention that it is a 12 1/2 gage [2.5 thick] smooth steel wire without specifying its tensile strength.",
      "According to Note 2, what is the required length range for the first leg of the 45 degree bend?": "10' to 13' [3 m to 4 m]",
      "According to Note H regarding Moisture Density Control (Cuts), what is the maximum depth specified for MDC below the ditch bottom?": "The maximum depth specified for Moisture Density Control (Cuts) below the ditch bottom is 2' [600].",
      "Based on Note 2, what action is required if the standard laying length of non-perforated pipe is greater than 13 ft [4 m]?": "If the standard laying length of non-perforated pipe is greater than 13 ft [4 m], cut the pipe to 10 ft [3 m] to form the first leg of the 45 degree bend.",
      "Does this sheet specify the exact hours of operation for the 'Daylight Hours Only' cone substitution rule?": "No, the sheet does not specify the exact hours of operation for the 'Daylight Hours Only' cone substitution rule.",
      "In the 'VALVE BOX COLLAR' plan view, what is the minimum distance from the outer diameter of the valve box to the edge of the concrete collar?": "6\" [150]",
      "What specified compressive strength (PSI) is listed for the 'Erosion Control Concrete' used in the stilling basin?": "The specified compressive strength for the 'Erosion Control Concrete' used in the stilling basin is not explicitly stated in the provided images. The plan only mentions that it is concrete and provides dimensions and other details but does not specify the compressive strength.",
      "In 'DETAIL A - HORIZONTAL STIFFENER WIRE CONNECTION', how many mesh vertical wires does the stiffener wire loop around?": "3",
      "Based on the 'TYPICAL SPEED REDUCTIONS' table, if the Posted Speed Limit is 65 MPH, what should the Reduced Speed Limit be?": "40 MPH",
      "In the 'STAKE SPACING TABLE', what is the required 'DOWN' spacing for a slope of 1V:3H?": "The required 'DOWN' spacing for a slope of 1V:3H in the 'STAKE SPACING TABLE' is 3.6 feet (1.08 meters).",
      "In the 'EDGE DRAIN (CONTINUOUS RUN)' diagram, which outlet type is used at the end of the run on the far right?": "In the 'EDGE DRAIN (CONTINUOUS RUN)' diagram, Outlet Type B is used at the end of the run on the far right.",
      "In 'SECTION A-A', what is the length of the flat bottom portion of the 'STILLING BASIN'?": "The length of the flat bottom portion of the 'STILLING BASIN' in 'SECTION A-A' is 12\" [305].",
      "Does the plan specify using a concrete footing for the steel stakes in the 'TYPICAL SECTION (FOR CHANNELS)'?": "No, the plan does not specify using a concrete footing for the steel stakes in the 'TYPICAL SECTION (FOR CHANNELS)'. The plan indicates that the stakes should be sloped to drain and compacted.",
      "Which specific traffic control device is represented by a  black vertical rectangular capsule in the 'LEGEND'?": "STOP",
      "In the 'CONCRETE HEADWALL' detail, what specific type of post is illustrated for the location post?": "The 'CONCRETE HEADWALL' detail illustrates a 'STEEL POST TYPE I DELINEATOR POST - NO BUTTON' as the specific type of post for the location post.",
      "What is the specified radius for the edge rounding shown in the detail bubble in valve box collar?": "1/4\" [5]",
      "According to the 'SIGN SPACING' table, what is the required sign spacing for speed limits of 40 MPH and Below?": "200 feet [60 meters]",
      "According to the 'EDGE DRAIN (CONTINUOUS RUN)' diagram, what is the maximum spacing between outlets?": "500 ft [150 m]",
      "How is the 'DRAINAGE AND FILTRATION FABRIC' depicted in the 'TYPICAL UNDERDRAIN DITCH' diagram?": "The 'DRAINAGE AND FILTRATION FABRIC' is depicted as a layer above the gravel for drains (grading B) and below the underdrain pipe in the 'TYPICAL UNDERDRAIN DITCH' diagram.",
      "Does the plan specify the trench width for the 'Edge Drain (Continuous Run)'?": "No, the plan does not specify the trench width for the 'Edge Drain (Continuous Run)'.",
      "According to the 'General Notes', what is the estimated quantity of riprap required for 1 SY [1 m\u00b2] of surface area?": "0.444 CY [0.400 m\u00b3]",
      "In the 'TYPICAL UNDERDRAIN DITCH' section, what is the minimum depth specified for the 'IMPERVIOUS MATERIAL' layer?": "8\" [205] (MIN.)",
      "Does the 'TYPICAL UNDERDRAIN DITCH' specify the material type (e.g., PVC, HDPE) for the 'UNDERDRAIN PIPE'?": "No, the 'TYPICAL UNDERDRAIN DITCH' does not specify the material type for the 'UNDERDRAIN PIPE'.",
      "In the diagram, what is the maximum spacing specified for taper drums?": "25' [8m]",
      "Based on the 'Estimated Riprap Quantities' note, if you have a surface area of 10 square meter, approximately how much riprap would be required?": "0.444 CY [0.400 m\u00b3] of riprap for 1 SY [1 m\u00b2] surface area. Therefore, for 10 square meters, you would need approximately 4.44 CY [4.00 m\u00b3] of riprap.",
      "Based on the note in the 'TYPICAL SECTION (FOR CHANNELS)', when is the toe section shown at the bottom of the slope NOT required?": "The toe section shown at the bottom of the slope is not required when riprap extends across the bottom of the channel.",
      "Does this sheet specify the specific gradation class (e.g., Class 1, Class 2) for the riprap stone?": "No, the sheet does not specify the specific gradation class for the riprap stone.",
      "Based on Note 3 regarding mid-block access, who is responsible for providing and placing channelizing devices?": "The contractor is responsible for providing and placing channelizing devices as required by Note 3 regarding mid-block access.",
      "In 'SECTION A-A (ADJACENT TO ASPHALT PAVEMENT)', what is the minimum collar depth specified?": "8\" [205] MIN.",
      "What is the  fill slope toe ditch speed  in Earthwork standard plan 203-2A?": "The fill slope toe ditch speed in Earthwork standard plan 203-2A is not explicitly stated in the provided image. The image focuses on grading notes and does not include specific speed information for the fill slope toe ditch.",
      "What specific ASTM standard is required for the retroreflective sheeting on the 'ROAD WORK AHEAD' signs?": "The specific ASTM standard required for the retroreflective sheeting on the 'ROAD WORK AHEAD' signs is not explicitly stated in the provided images. However, typically, such standards would be referenced in the detailed specifications or construction plans which are not included here. For accurate information, one should refer to the full set of construction plans and specifications provided by WYDOT.",
      "According to the 'LEGEND', which symbol represents a 'DRUM WITH SIGN' in construction and traffic control two lane?": "The symbol that represents a 'DRUM WITH SIGN' in construction and traffic control for a two-lane road according to the 'LEGEND' is a black circle (\u25cf) with a white square inside it.",
      "Based on the text in the 'CUT SECTION' diagram, what is the required compaction percentage for the material backfilled to subgrade?": "The required compaction percentage for the material backfilled to subgrade is not less than 95% of maximum.",
      "According to the 'TYPICAL PLAN NORMAL TO SLOPE', what is the exact vertical spacing for the steel stakes in the center of each enclosure?": "The exact vertical spacing for the steel stakes in the center of each enclosure, as per the 'TYPICAL PLAN NORMAL TO SLOPE', is 4'-10\" [1.5 m].",
      "In 'SECTION A-A (TIE TO CONCRETE PAVEMENT)', what determines the depth of the concrete collar?": "The depth of the concrete collar in 'SECTION A-A (TIE TO CONCRETE PAVEMENT)' is determined by the thickness of the concrete pavement.",
      "Does the plan specify the concrete mix class (e.g., Class B, Class 4000) for the valve box collar?": "No, the plan does not specify the concrete mix class for the valve box collar.",
      "In the 'EDGE DRAIN (SAG LOCATION)' detail, what is the dimension shown for the spacing between the two Type C outlets?": "2'-6\" [760]",
      "According to Note 2, what is the minimum traveled way width required between channelizing devices?": "10 feet [3 m]",
      "In the 'SIDEHILL CUT & FILL SECTION', how is the boundary between the fill slope and the existing ground labeled when the slope is steep?": "The boundary between the fill slope and the existing ground in the 'SIDEHILL CUT & FILL SECTION' is labeled as \"BENCH AS REQUIRED WHEN EXISTING SLOPE STEEPER THAN 1V:4H.\"",
      "Which specific section detail depicts both a 'Barnroof Design' and a 'Flat Slope Design'?": "The 'Sidehill Cut & Fill Section' detail depicts both a 'Barnroof Design' and a 'Flat Slope Design'.",
      "In the 'TYPICAL PLAN (FOR RC CULVERTS)', how are the steel stakes and wire tie graphically represented within the grid and what does the plus represent?": "In the 'TYPICAL PLAN (FOR RC CULVERTS)', the steel stakes are represented by the plus signs (+) within the grid, and the wire ties are also shown as plus signs (+). The plus sign represents the placement of these elements at specific intervals within the grid.",
      "What is the typical offset distance from the edge of the pavement to the underdrain pipe (perforated) shown in the 'EDGE DRAIN (SAG LOCATION)' detail?": "1' - 0\" [0.3 m]",
      "In the 'EXPANDED VIEW' diagram, where are the wire ties located relative to the V-mesh end strips?": "The wire ties are located at the top of the V-mesh end strips in the 'EXPANDED VIEW' diagram.",
      "In the 'LACING DETAIL FOR WIRE ENCLOSED RIPRAP', what is the size of the mesh opening for the V-Mesh?": "The size of the mesh opening for the V-Mesh in the 'LACING DETAIL FOR WIRE ENCLOSED RIPRAP' is 2\" x 4\".",
      "According to Grading Note D, where specifically should Contour Ditches be located in earthwork standard plans?": "Above the point of intersection between the backslope and the original ground line at sites having a drainage area of sufficient size where surface runoff would erode the backslope.",
      "What is the maximum distance to the first row of stakes shown in the 'TYPICAL SECTION (FOR CHANNELS)'?": "23'-0\" [7.1 m]",
      "What is the specified depth for scarifying the surface as indicated in the 'FILL SECTION' detail and Note I?": "6 inches [150]",
      "According to the 'General Notes' for wire enclosed riprap steel stakes, under what specific slope condition are steel stakes required?": "Steel stakes are required on slopes that are 1V:2H and steeper.",
      "In the 'VALVE BOX COLLAR' plan view, how is the concrete collar oriented relative to the traffic direction?": "The concrete collar in the 'VALVE BOX COLLAR' plan view is oriented perpendicular to the traffic direction.",
      "According to the notes under the 'STAKE SPACING TABLE', where should stakes be placed relative to the unit connections?": "Stakes should be placed near the connections of units when possible.",
      "What specific ASTM standard is listed for the 'Suitable Material' mentioned in the backfill notes?": "The specific ASTM standard listed for the 'Suitable Material' mentioned in the backfill notes is ASTM A569.",
      "According to the 'GUIDELINES FOR TAPER LENGTHS' table, what is the required Taper Length (L) for a speed limit of 45 MPH?": "540 feet [160 meters]",
      "What specific type of joint sealant is specified for the 'TIE TO CONCRETE PAVEMENT' section in valve box collars?": "The 'TIE TO CONCRETE PAVEMENT' section specifies the use of standard joint sealant.",
      "How is the 'Geotextile Erosion Control (Fabric)' depicted in the 'TYPICAL SECTION (FOR RC CULVERTS)'?": "The 'Geotextile Erosion Control (Fabric)' is depicted as a layer placed under the entire surface area of riprap in the 'TYPICAL SECTION (FOR RC CULVERTS)'.",
      "Based on General Note 1, when are concrete valve box collars required?": "Concrete valve box collars are required for new valve boxes and where adjusting existing valve boxes.",
      "What specific ASTM standard is listed for the 'Double-Twist Wire Netting' material properties?": "The specific ASTM standard listed for the 'Double-Twist Wire Netting' material properties is AASHTO M181.",
      "Based on the 'Gabion and Revet Mattress Construction' notes, are horizontal stiffener wires required for 1 ft [0.3 m] high gabions?": "No, horizontal stiffener wires are not required for 1 ft [0.3 m] high gabions.",
      "According to Note 1, what is the purpose of using different types of channelizing devices on each side of the traveled way?": "To reduce motorist confusion.",
      "In the 'OUTLET PIPE CONNECTIONS' detail, what two components are shown connecting the perforated pipe to the non-perforated pipe for a wye connection?": "The two components shown connecting the perforated pipe to the non-perforated pipe for a wye connection in the 'OUTLET PIPE CONNECTIONS' detail are:\n\n1. 45\u00b0 WYE\n2. 45\u00b0 ELBOW"
    },
